BEHAVIOR processed-marker

DESCRIPTION
  Emits " PROCESSED BY CONSUMER\n" as a null-terminated bytes buffer.
  This exists because `concat` finds a sequence's length by scanning for a
  null terminator, and a string literal can no longer be fed to it: string
  literals are now length-prefixed ([8-byte len][content], reference 2.5),
  so concat reads the length-prefix bytes as content and stops at the first
  zero inside them. Emitting the marker as explicit null-terminated bytes
  keeps the original byte-oriented concat pipeline correct.

CONTRACT
  OUTPUT marker bytes 32
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH 3eacf937

IMPLEMENTATION
  STORE marker 32 1 0
  STORE marker 80 1 1
  STORE marker 82 1 2
  STORE marker 79 1 3
  STORE marker 67 1 4
  STORE marker 69 1 5
  STORE marker 83 1 6
  STORE marker 83 1 7
  STORE marker 69 1 8
  STORE marker 68 1 9
  STORE marker 32 1 10
  STORE marker 66 1 11
  STORE marker 89 1 12
  STORE marker 32 1 13
  STORE marker 67 1 14
  STORE marker 79 1 15
  STORE marker 78 1 16
  STORE marker 83 1 17
  STORE marker 85 1 18
  STORE marker 77 1 19
  STORE marker 69 1 20
  STORE marker 82 1 21
  STORE marker 10 1 22
  STORE marker 0 1 23
END
